.TH DEV-RUN 1 "2026-10-12" "cti-agent 1.3" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
dev-run \- run the CTI pipeline from a repository checkout, stage by stage, for testing and debugging
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fleet\-kit/bin/dev\-run
.RI [ stage ]
.RB [ \-\-provider
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-to
.IR ADDRESS ]
.RB [ \-\-for\-real ]
.PP
.I stage
is one of
.BR doctor ,
.BR ingest ,
.BR enrich ,
.BR brief ,
.BR send ,
.BR all .
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dev\-run
runs the daily pipeline on a developer's Mac or Linux machine, from a
checkout, with no root, no service account and no systemd. It answers one
question: does this read the mailbox and produce believable threat intel?
It is run by a developer, never by a timer, and is not installed on the
fleet box.
.PP
It finds the repository from its own location, reads the Go agent's
.I .env
at the repository root (exported with
.BR "set \-a" ),
and keeps everything it generates in
.I .fleet\-local/
inside the repository, which is gitignored: the report, the enriched JSON,
the digest, logs, the findings database, the NVD and KEV caches and the
built agent. Hostnames are written in full unless
.B REPORT_HOSTNAMES
says otherwise.
.PP
Nothing is sent except by the
.B send
stage, and that is a dry run unless
.B \-\-for\-real
is given. Every other stage is read-only toward the outside world, apart
from the API queries enrichment makes.
.SH COMMANDS
Each stage can be run on its own, to see where the pipeline breaks; a stage
reads the previous stage's output for today's date. With no stage,
.B all
is run.
.TP
.B doctor
Checks that
.B go
and
.B python3
are installed; that
.BR TENANT_ID ,
.BR CLIENT_ID ,
.B CLIENT_SECRET
and
.B GRAPH_MAILBOX
are set (the secret's length is shown, never its value); the Qualys
credentials when the provider is
.BR qualys ;
and then runs
.B "mailer.py \-\-check"
and interprets it: no token is a hard failure, with a hint telling a network
or TLS-inspecting proxy problem apart from rejected credentials; a missing
.B Mail.Read
is a hard failure; a missing
.B Mail.Send
is a warning, because only
.B send
needs it. Ends with
.B ready
or
.BR "fix the above before continuing" .
.IP
The role test matches
.B "MISSING Mail.Read"
and
.B "MISSING Mail.Send"
with one space, and
.B "mailer.py \-\-check"
prints two, so a missing role is not caught and the stage reports both
granted. It reports the same when
.B FLEET_OPERATOR_EMAIL
is unset, because
.B \-\-check
then stops before requesting a token. Read the
.B \-\-check
lines it prints above the verdict.
.TP
.B ingest
Always rebuilds the Go agent
.RB ( "go build ./cmd/cti\-agent" ,
near-instant when nothing changed) into
.IR .fleet\-local/cti\-agent\-dev ,
says which commit it was built from and whether uncommitted
.I .go
changes were included, runs it with its report directed to
.IR .fleet\-local/reports/raw\-YYYY\-MM\-DD.md ,
and summarises the CVE rows by status. The
.B "emails inspected"
line looks for a label the agent no longer writes and shows
.BR ? .
When no CVE was extracted it lists
what to check, in order.
.TP
.B enrich
Runs
.BR enrich.py (1)
on today's report into
.IR .fleet\-local/state/enriched\-YYYY\-MM\-DD.json ,
which also upserts the findings into
.IR .fleet\-local/state/memory.db ,
then tries to print the band counts and the top findings. That summary
reads counts named
.BR P1 \(en P4 ,
which
.B enrich.py
no longer writes, so it fails with a Python
.B KeyError
after the enriched file is written, and the run ends with status 1; under
.B all
the brief stage is never reached. Run
.B brief
on its own afterwards.
.TP
.B brief
Runs
.BR brief.py (1)
.B \-\-daily
into
.I .fleet\-local/reports/digest\-YYYY\-MM\-DD.html
and
.IR .txt ,
prints the subject and the first 28 lines of the text version. Sends
nothing.
.TP
.B send
Mails today's digest with
.BR mailer.py (1),
to
.BR \-\-to ,
else
.BR DIGEST_TO .
It first runs
.B "mailer.py \-\-check"
and stops if
.B Mail.Send
is reported missing. The allowlist is set to exactly the recipient
.RB ( FLEET_ALLOW_TO
is exported as that address), so the real gate runs rather than being
bypassed with
.BR \-\-approve .
The raw report is attached. Without
.B \-\-for\-real
the mailer is run with
.BR \-\-dry\-run .
.TP
.B all
.BR doctor ,
whose failure does not stop the run, then
.BR ingest ,
.B enrich
and
.BR brief ,
then opens the digest with
.BR open (1)
on macOS or
.BR xdg\-open (1)
on Linux, or prints its path. Never sends.
.SH OPTIONS
Options follow the stage.
.TP
.BI \-\-provider " NAME"
Exported as
.B LOOKUP_PROVIDER
for this run, overriding
.IR .env .
.B none
skips the scanner and proves Graph access and CVE extraction alone;
.B qualys
uses Qualys.
.TP
.BI \-\-to " ADDRESS"
Recipient for
.BR send .
Ignored by every other stage.
.TP
.B \-\-for\-real
Make
.B send
actually send.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Values in
.I .env
are exported and replace variables of the same name already in the
environment.
.TP
.B FLEET_HOME
Where generated files go.
Default:\~\fI<repo>/.fleet\-local\fR. Set before
.I .env
is read, and the output paths are fixed from it then. A
.B FLEET_HOME=
line in
.I .env
(as in
.IR .env.example )
still replaces it with an empty value for the lanes, which then put their
caches and
.I memory.db
under
.I ./state
in the current directory.
.TP
.BR TENANT_ID ", " CLIENT_ID ", " CLIENT_SECRET ", " GRAPH_MAILBOX
Required by
.BR doctor ;
used by the agent and the mailer.
.TP
.BR QUALYS_BASE_URL ", " QUALYS_USERNAME ", " QUALYS_PASSWORD
Required by
.B doctor
when the provider is
.BR qualys .
.TP
.B LOOKUP_PROVIDER
Scanner. Default:\~\fBqualys\fR.
.TP
.B GRAPH_LOOKBACK_HOURS
Mailbox window, shown by
.B doctor
and
.BR ingest .
Default:\~\fB24\fR.
.TP
.B GRAPH_FOLDER
Mailbox folder, read by the agent.
.TP
.B REPORT_PATH
Always set to today's
.I raw
report in
.IR .fleet\-local/reports ,
whatever
.I .env
says.
.TP
.B REPORT_HOSTNAMES
.BR full ,
.B redact
or
.BR count .
Default:\~\fBfull\fR.
.TP
.B QUALYS_KB_CACHE
Default:\~\fI$FLEET_HOME/state/qualys_kb_cache.json\fR.
.TP
.B NVD_API_KEY
Passed to
.BR enrich.py ;
unset, the enrich stage warns that it may take minutes.
.TP
.B DIGEST_TO
Recipient for
.B send
when
.B \-\-to
is not given.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <repo>/.env
The Go agent's settings, required; copy
.I .env.example
to start.
.TP
.I <repo>/.fleet\-local/reports/raw\-YYYY\-MM\-DD.md
The agent's report.
.TP
.I <repo>/.fleet\-local/state/enriched\-YYYY\-MM\-DD.json
Enriched findings.
.TP
.I <repo>/.fleet\-local/reports/digest\-YYYY\-MM\-DD.{html,txt}
The rendered digest.
.TP
.I <repo>/.fleet\-local/logs/ingest.log
The agent's output from the last
.BR ingest .
.TP
.I <repo>/.fleet\-local/cti\-agent\-dev
The binary
.B ingest
built.
.TP
.I <repo>/.fleet\-local/state/memory.db
Findings history, written by the enrich stage.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The stage, or every stage of
.BR all ,
finished. A dry-run
.B send
that passed the gate is 0.
.TP
.B 1
.I .env
is missing; a stage failed (doctor found a problem, the build failed, no
report or enriched file was produced, the enrich summary failed, a
needed earlier output is missing,
no recipient for
.BR send ,
Mail.Send missing, or the mailer refused); or an option was given without
its value.
.TP
.B 2
Unknown option or unknown stage; a usage line is printed.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start with configuration and permissions, then prove mail reading without
the scanner:
.PP
.EX
fleet\-kit/bin/dev\-run doctor
fleet\-kit/bin/dev\-run ingest \-\-provider none
.EE
.PP
The full pipeline, opening the digest at the end:
.PP
.EX
fleet\-kit/bin/dev\-run all
.EE
.PP
Send the digest to yourself: first the dry run, then for real:
.PP
.EX
fleet\-kit/bin/dev\-run send \-\-to you@example.com
fleet\-kit/bin/dev\-run send \-\-to you@example.com \-\-for\-real
.EE
.PP
Widen the window when nothing was extracted:
.PP
.EX
GRAPH_LOOKBACK_HOURS=168 fleet\-kit/bin/dev\-run ingest
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR enrich.py (1),
.BR brief.py (1),
.BR mailer.py (1),
.BR fleet\-db (1),
.BR run\-digest (1)
.PP
RUNBOOK.md section 6; fleet\-kit/README.md, "Test it locally first".
